From: Adriel Santos <adriel@adriel.eu>
Subject: [PATCH] nss: an8855: support bridge VLAN filtering under tag_8021q (layered after 999-2757)

Enabling vlan_filtering on the NSS build silently killed the DSA host
path and kept it dead until reboot. an8855_port_vlan_filtering() is the
stock mt7530-derived implementation with no tag_8021q awareness, and on
enable it reprograms the *upstream* port:

	an8855_port_set_vlan_mode(priv, dsa_upstream_port(ds, port),
				  AN8855_PORT_FALLBACK_MODE,
				  AN8855_VLAN_EG_CONSISTENT, ...)

EG_CONSISTENT means "untagged in, untagged out", which overrides the
per-VID egress-tag field an8855_vlan_add() sets for CPU ports and is the
exact opposite of what an8855_setup() installs (EG_DISABLED, so the VLAN
table decides). The conduit then receives frames carrying no VLAN header,
the vsc73xx-8021q tagger has no VID to decode, and RX dies for every user
port sharing that CPU port - bridged or not. TX survives, so the box
keeps being learned upstream while being unreachable. The disable path
wrote EG_CONSISTENT too and never restored the tag_8021q programming,
which is why `uci revert` did not recover the box, only a reboot did.

Measured on an RD03v2 AP (tagger vsc73xx-8021q, conduit port 5) via the
an8855_dsa netlink interface, enabling vlan_filtering on br-lan changed
exactly one field on the whole switch:

	PVC_P(5) 0x91000000 -> 0x91000100   (PVC_EG_TAG 0 -> 1)
	ping 192.168.1.1: 2/2 -> 0/2

and writing PVC_P(5) back to 0x91000000 restored the host path live,
with no reboot: 2/2, br-lan.1 up with its address, NSS still loaded.

So follow the mainline model for a driver that commits the tag_8021q
VLAN as a PVID (net/dsa/tag_8021q.c):

 - Never touch CPU-port PVC_EG_TAG outside an8855_setup(). The CPU port
   stays a tagged member of every bridge VLAN, which an8855_vlan_add()
   already arranges, and the VLAN table keeps deciding egress tagging.

 - Add per-port shadow PVIDs (pvid_tag_8021q, pvid_bridge) and an
   an8855_port_commit_vlan() that programs whichever the port's current
   VLAN-awareness selects, like sja1105_commit_pvid() and
   vsc73xx_vlan_commit_pvid(). .tag_8021q_vlan_add/_del and
   .port_vlan_add/_del now only update their own shadow and commit, so
   the two writers stop clobbering the single PVID register pair and
   leaving a VLAN-aware bridge restores the tag_8021q PVID without a
   reboot. .port_vlan_filtering becomes just that commit.

   vlan_filtering is passed to the commit explicitly rather than read
   back: DSA assigns dp->vlan_filtering only after .port_vlan_filtering
   returns (dsa_port_vlan_filtering(), net/dsa/port.c), so the port still
   reports the old state during the callback.

 - Reject bridge VLANs in 3072-4095 from .port_vlan_add, as
   sja1105_vlan_add() and vsc73xx_port_vlan_add() do; otherwise a user
   VLAN can rewrite the entries tag_8021q identifies source ports with.

 - Fix the inverted accept-frame test carried over from the mt7530
   original: it read "PVID set -> accept tagged only", the opposite of
   its own comment and of mt7530.c, so a trunk-only port with no PVID
   got ACC_ALL and classified untagged ingress into VID 0.

Source-port precision is conceded under a VLAN-aware bridge - frames
arrive with the bridge VID and dsa_find_designated_bridge_port_by_vid()
resolves them - which is what net/dsa/tag_8021q.c documents for this
class of driver and what the vsc73xx-8021q tagger already expects
(vsc73xx_xmit() returns the skb untouched when br_vlan_enabled()).

Layered after 999-2757 (add an8855 v2p0p1 + netlink) for the same reason
as 999-2758 and 999-2759: that patch rewrites hunks inside
an8855_port_vlan_filtering() and an8855_port_vlan_add() on top of the
files overlay, so editing the overlay's copy makes it fail to apply.
NSS-only; the base MTK-tag build is unaffected, since its special tag
carries the source port independently of the VLAN table.

The reserved-range rejection logs as well as filling in the extack. The
extack only reaches whoever issued the netlink request, so with such a VID
in /etc/config/network the only visible symptom is netifd retrying the
bridge join and eventually leaving every user port out of the bridge, with
nothing in dmesg explaining why.

Link: https://github.com/ADCDS/openwrt-xiaomi-ax3000t-rd03v2/issues/11

