+ * Commit a user port's VLAN classification from the software shadow state.
+ *
+ * AN8855_PPBV1_P/AN8855_PVID_P hold one PVID per port, but two subsystems
+ * want to own it. tag_8021q needs its standalone (or bridge) VID there, so
+ * that untagged ingress is classified into the VID that identifies the source
+ * port to the conduit tagger; a VLAN-aware bridge needs the user's own PVID.
+ * They cannot coexist, so - like sja1105_commit_pvid() and
+ * vsc73xx_vlan_commit_pvid() - keep both in software and let the port's
+ * VLAN-awareness arbitrate. Every writer updates its shadow and commits here;
+ * nothing pokes the PVID registers directly.
+ *
+ * vlan_filtering is passed in rather than read back from
+ * dsa_port_is_vlan_filtering(), because DSA only assigns dp->vlan_filtering
+ * *after* .port_vlan_filtering returns (dsa_port_vlan_filtering(),
+ * net/dsa/port.c) - during that callback the port still reports the old state.
+ *
+ * Under a VLAN-aware bridge source-port precision is conceded, exactly as
+ * net/dsa/tag_8021q.c describes for drivers that commit the tag_8021q VLAN as
+ * a PVID: frames reach software carrying the bridge VID rather than a
+ * tag_8021q VID, and dsa_find_designated_bridge_port_by_vid() resolves them
+ * imprecisely. That is the documented tradeoff, not a regression.
